  "raw": "en Español\n\n000\nABNT20 KNHC 311756\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 PM EDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on newly formed \nTropical Depression Five, located over the northern Gulf of America.\n\nNear Hispaniola (Remnants of Dolly):\nA surface trough of low pressure (the remnants of Tropical Storm \nDolly) is producing disorganized showers and thunderstorms near and \nover portions of Hispaniola, Turks and Caicos, and the southeastern \nBahamas. Significant development of this system is no longer \nexpected while it moves west-northwestward at 15 to 20 mph over the \nsouthwestern Atlantic. Regardless, the system could bring locally \nheavy rains and gusty winds to portions of these areas during the \nnext couple of days.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...near 0 percent.\n\n&&\nPublic Advisories on Tropical Depression Five are issued under WMO \nheader WTNT35 KNHC and under AWIPS header MIATCPAT5.\nForecast/Advisories on Tropical Depression Five are issued under WMO \nheader WTNT25 KNHC and under AWIPS header MIATCMAT5.\n\n$$\nForecaster Reinhart"
